From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:41:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 67/67] Plot: interactive layer offset without negating INT_MIN

PlotInteractiveLayer() negated the plot offset, which is INT_MIN for a
footprint whose box reaches the edge of the coordinate range (UBSan: negation
of -2147483648 in vector2d.h:505, fp export svg). Negate in 64 bits and clamp.

Found by tools/bughunt (kicad-ja-plus, run 39129160714).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 pcbnew/plot_board_layers.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pcbnew/plot_board_layers.cpp b/pcbnew/plot_board_layers.cpp
index 9a1f44040..4ce5e5763 100644
--- a/pcbnew/plot_board_layers.cpp
+++ b/pcbnew/plot_board_layers.cpp
@@ -196,7 +196,10 @@ void PlotInteractiveLayer( BOARD* aBoard, PLOTTER* aPlotter, const PCB_PLOT_PARA
 #endif
         // Draw items are plotted with a position offset. So we need to move
         // our boxes (which are not plotted) by the same offset.
-        VECTOR2I offset = -aPlotter->GetPlotOffsetUserUnits();
+        // In 64 bits, clamped: the offset can be INT_MIN, whose negation does not fit
+        const VECTOR2I plotOffset = aPlotter->GetPlotOffsetUserUnits();
+        VECTOR2I       offset( int( std::min<int64_t>( -int64_t( plotOffset.x ), std::numeric_limits<int>::max() ) ),
+                               int( std::min<int64_t>( -int64_t( plotOffset.y ), std::numeric_limits<int>::max() ) ) );
 
         // Use a footprint bbox without texts to create the hyperlink area
         BOX2I bbox = fp->GetBoundingBox( false );
